{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/991242-stick-with-the-canon-or-change-it-completely","id":991242,"title":"Stick with the Canon or Change it completely?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-21T20:34:55-07:00","id":991242,"title":"Stick with the Canon or Change it completely?","content":"So, i been wondering a lot about this. I started to make my own canon set in 1875 with a massive alliance against the forces of the wyrm.<br /> i told an old timer player of werewolf and she was disgusted to say the least.<br /> <br /> i been thinking a lot about it. my players are having a lot of fun (even if they are newcommers) but i feel..dunno...shame? of ripping the canon a new one..ever went through something like this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T21:15:40-07:00","id":991260,"title":"","content":"White Wolf has always advocated the golden rule of &quot;fun comes first; everything else is secondary&quot; and what I like to call the &quot;silver rule&quot; of &quot;take what you like about our material and toss out everything else.&quot; In other words, don't feel ashamed; if your players are having a fun time then you're doing it right as a storyteller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T21:20:58-07:00","id":991266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/991242-stick-with-the-canon-or-change-it-completely?p=991260#post991260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">White Wolf has always advocated the golden rule of &quot;fun comes first; everything else is secondary&quot; and what I like to call the &quot;silver rule&quot; of &quot;take what you like about our material and toss out everything else.&quot; In other words, don't feel ashamed; if your players are having a fun time then you're doing it right as a storyteller.</div> </div> </div> </div>even if other dm's point me with the finger and the &quot;How Dare you&quot; stick?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T22:08:17-07:00","id":991278,"title":"","content":"Your game your rules.<br /> Until the Tribebook White Howler came out every other version of the Fall of the White Howlers made no sense. I have allowed the White Howlers to be played for years. Yes I use BSD but use them sparingly for good reason. BSD should be the fear of the traitor the trusted companion who betrays the hero(s) at the perfect moment. The Wyrm does not need slobbering idiot servants it has plenty of them it needs reasoning rational corruption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T22:22:06-07:00","id":991281,"title":"","content":"It's your game, go nuts with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T01:32:51-07:00","id":991307,"title":"","content":"100% do it your way. White Wolf deliberately built a world where you can take as much or as little of the metaplot as you wish and that's part of why so many of us love it so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","name":"ElizabethSterling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5445_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T17:30:39-07:00","id":991617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/991242-stick-with-the-canon-or-change-it-completely#post991242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, i been wondering a lot about this. I started to make my own canon set in 1875 with a massive alliance against the forces of the wyrm.<br /> i told an old timer player of werewolf and she was disgusted to say the least.<br /> <br /> i been thinking a lot about it. my players are having a lot of fun (even if they are newcommers) but i feel..dunno...shame? of ripping the canon a new one..ever went through something like this?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's your table and your group's game so don't feel shame for having fun as long as the rest of the group is loving it too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T17:48:54-07:00","id":991624,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there is no reason to not have alternative histories, just try to keep them internally consistent so you do not confuse your players too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T13:13:50-07:00","id":991979,"title":"","content":"The only rule you should (and apparently did) follow is to tell your players what you're doing.<br /> <br /> And yes, WoD fandom in most places is sadly overcrowded with puritan a**holes. We have a lot here in Brazil. Forget about that and do the canon that works for you. The official canon doesn't work for most people, eitherway, so who cares? It is only relevant when you want to discuss setting with people (because we need common ground to start), and even then you can throw your thing in the middle if you want and everyone's ok with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}